      "id": "q_000003",
      "question_type": "mcq",
      "question": {
        "text": "If a train traveling at 60 km/h crosses a pole in 9 seconds, what is the length of the train?"
      },
      "options": [
        {"id": "A", "text": "120 meters"},
        {"id": "B", "text": "150 meters"},
        {"id": "C", "text": "180 meters"},
        {"id": "D", "text": "200 meters"}
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct_option": "B",
        "correct_text": "150 meters"
      },
      "explanation": "Speed = 60 km/h = 60 * (5/18) m/s = 50/3 m/s. \nDistance (length of train) = Speed * Time = (50/3) * 9 = 150 meters.",
